# NOTE (build-time, ground-check vs ship reality): the gate's extractor matches a
# field followed by a ":" or "=" separator (extract_author_fields, OLD + new cfg
# branch are byte-identical). The classic LICENSE form "Copyright (c) 2026 Name"
# has NO such separator and is therefore NOT matched by the gate (a pre-existing
# property, unrelated to the Arc 65 narrowing). This fixture uses the "Copyright:"
# separator form so it exercises the LICENSE-class cfg BLOCK path the design
# intends. See ADA's return-message drift note.
